**Ghazal: The Plot Will Unfold in Real Time**

At dusk, the city kneels beneath a sky of crime in real time;  
The plot will unfold in real time.

Burning bodies flower where the checkpoints bloom and climb in real time;  
Smoke writes its black scripture, line after line, in real time.

Our prayers came unwound from the beads of the old shrine in real time;  
God listened through static, through ash, through a broken chime in real time.

In the rearview mirror, my childhood kept waving goodbye in real time;  
The road swallowed my name with its mouth full of lime in real time.

Faith was a lantern I carried through bullets and brine in real time;  
Loneliness ate its flame, sublime by sublime, in real time.

Mother, forgive me: I left before dawn’s first sign in real time;  
I learned farewell is a wound that refuses to rhyme in real time.

The soldiers were boys with thunder stitched into their spine in real time;  
They sang to stay human while crossing the line in real time.

O heart, do not ask why the stars taste of iodine in real time;  
Heaven has bandaged its gates for the dying in real time.

And I, last witness, turn my face from the divine in real time;  
Still, I whisper farewell—mine, mine, mine—in real time.
